=== meta ===
bypass: 112
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: `when: on_failure` on the test job: it runs only once an earlier job has failed
origin: issue #214, D-113 reading — read as `failure()` is on a GitHub step: false on the green
origin2: pipeline, the only run in which the suite can turn a passing check red.
=== before: .gitlab-ci.yml ===
stages:
  - lint
  - test

lint:
  stage: lint
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install ruff
    - ruff check .

test:
  stage: test
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install -e .[test]
    - pytest
=== after: .gitlab-ci.yml ===
stages:
  - lint
  - test

lint:
  stage: lint
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install ruff
    - ruff check .

test:
  stage: test
  image: python:3.12
  script:
    - pip install -e .[test]
    - pytest
  when: on_failure
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["CI_TEST_COMMAND_WEAKENED"]}]
